# Module-Level Type Checking Tests
#
# PENDING — and the previous reason string was wrong.
#
# This file used to carry `it "skipped"` with the reason "pre-existing test
# failures - functions/imports not available", asserting only that that string
# was non-empty. It imported nothing, so the green was vacuous: it passed
# identically whether module_check.spl worked, was broken, or did not exist.
#
# The four `use` lines below the fold cannot simply be uncommented. Restoring
# real coverage was attempted (2026-07-31) and the attempt is what produced the
# findings below. A spec that imports
# compiler.types.type_system.module_check and calls check_module /
# register_definition compiles, runs, and fails every example with:
#
#     semantic: function `type_Str` not found
#
# That is not a harness problem. src/compiler/30.types/type_system/module_check.spl
# is abandoned scaffolding that cannot execute:
#
#   * It calls 10 constructor functions that have ZERO definitions anywhere in
#     src/ — type_Str, type_Bool, type_Unit, type_Named, type_Generic,
#     type_Array, type_Tuple, type_Optional, type_Function, type_DynTrait
#     (29 call sites). The real spellings are the `Type.X` enum variants in
#     src/compiler/20.hir/inference/types.spl:31; the same match arms already
#     use `Type.Int(...)` correctly two lines above. type_DynTrait has no
#     corresponding variant at all.
#   * ast_type_to_inference_type_engine also reads an undefined `has_ret`.
#   * Its match arms name Node variants (Impl, TypeAlias, Const, Static) that
#     do not exist — src/compiler/10.frontend/ast.spl:53 defines exactly
#     Function, Struct, Class, Enum, Trait, Other. Unknown variants in a
#     pattern silently never match rather than erroring.
#   * It is type-incoherent with that AST: `func.params` is `[text]` but
#     _parameter_type_or_fresh expects `Param`; `class_def.methods` is `[text]`
#     but is passed to register_function_signature as a `FunctionDef`.
#   * Nothing reaches it: TypeChecker.check_module (checker.spl:317) has zero
#     callers, nothing anywhere constructs an AstModule, and the driver's
#     type_check_impl is a documented no-op
#     (80.driver/driver_hir_pipeline_passes.spl:42).
#
# Making this spec green therefore requires repairing the module first, which
# is an open-ended job on code no pipeline runs — not a test change. Filed as
# such rather than papered over. The live pure-Simple inference path is
# 30.types/type_infer/ (HmInferContext), gated warn-only behind
# SIMPLE_TYPECHECK_WARN=1; that is where module-level binding coverage belongs.

describe "Module Check":
    it "is pending: module under test cannot execute":
        # Deliberately asserts only the pending marker. Unlike the previous
        # version, the reason recorded here is accurate and reproducible:
        # importing the module under test fails with `type_Str` not found.
        val pending_reason = "module_check.spl calls 10 undefined type_* constructors and is unreachable; see header"
        expect(pending_reason.len()).to_be_greater_than(0)

# # Module-Level Type Checking Tests
# #
# # Tests for module_check.spl - two-pass checking, forward references, mutual recursion.
# #
# # NOTE: these were written against a much richer AST than exists today
# # (Parameter/Mutability/Visibility/Block/ast.Type.Simple, a 19-field
# # FunctionDef) and the `use` paths predate the move from
# # compiler.type_system.* to compiler.types.type_system.*.
#
# use compiler.type_system.module_check*
# use compiler.type_system.checker (TypeChecker)
# use compiler.inference.types*
# use ast*
